The total cost is  

\[
\begin{aligned}
\text{Donuts} &: 3 \text{ dozen} \times \$68/\text{dozen}= \$204 \\
\text{Mini cupcakes} &: 2 \text{ dozen} \times \$80/\text{dozen}= \$160 \\
\text{Mini cheesecakes} &: 6 \text{ dozen} \times \$55/\text{dozen}= \$330 \\
\hline
\text{Total} &: 204 + 160 + 330 = \boxed{\$694}
\end{aligned}
\]

Lee’s time is 38 s, which is 2 s faster than Gerald’s original time.

\[
\text{Gerald’s original time}=38\text{ s}+2\text{ s}=40\text{ s}
\]

Gerald’s speed then increases by 10 %.  
Since speed \(v = \dfrac{\text{distance}}{\text{time}}\),

\[
\text{new speed}=1.10 \times \text{original speed}
\]

\[
\text{new time}= \frac{\text{distance}}{\text{new speed}}
               = \frac{\text{distance}}{1.10\,(\text{distance}/\text{original time})}
               = \frac{\text{original time}}{1.10}
\]

\[
\text{Gerald’s improved time}= \frac{40\text{ s}}{1.10}= \frac{400}{11}\text{ s}
                              \approx 36.36\text{ s}
\]

\[
\boxed{\,\approx 36.36\text{ seconds}\,}
\]

Winston’s total cost is  

\[
\begin{aligned}
\text{Peaches} &: 6\text{ lb} \times \$2.00/\text{lb} = \$12.00 \\
\text{Plums}   &: 8\text{ lb} \times \$1.00/\text{lb} = \$8.00 \\
\text{Apricots}&: 6\text{ lb} \times \$3.00/\text{lb} = \$18.00 \\
\hline
\text{Total}   &: \$12.00 + \$8.00 + \$18.00 = \boxed{\$38.00}
\end{aligned}
\]

First, find each contestant’s total spitting distance.

- **Zoey:** 40 seeds × 10 ft/seed = **400 ft**
- **Sydney:** 35 seeds × 12 ft/seed = **420 ft**

Now average the two totals:

\[
\text{Average total distance} = \frac{400\text{ ft} + 420\text{ ft}}{2}
= \frac{820\text{ ft}}{2}
= \mathbf{410\text{ ft}}
\]

**Answer: 410 feet**.

Patty’s total charge is  

\[
\begin{aligned}
\text{Visit fee} &= \$40 \\[4pt]
\text{Labor (2.25 h → 3 h)} &= 3 \times \$35 = \$105 \\[4pt]
\text{Parts} &= \$60 \\[4pt]
\text{Total} &= 40 + 105 + 60 = \boxed{\$205}
\end{aligned}
\]

The average shoe size is  

\[
\frac{\text{Sophie’s size} + \text{Charlie’s size}}{2}
= \frac{5 + 5\cdot 5}{2}
= \frac{5 + 25}{2}
= \frac{30}{2}
= 15.
\]

**Answer: 15**
